    "answer": "The core anatomy has held up. Harvey's account of the heart driving blood out through the arteries and back by the veins [B5] matches the modern description of the circulation [W5].\n\nThe observation that drawn blood separates into a clot and a yellowish serum [B2] is still how serum is defined, under the same name [W6].\n\nThe red globules seen through Leeuwenhoek's microscope [B3] are today's red blood cells [W2]: the fact survived, the name did not.",
